tracee: let the kernel kill every tracee when proot ends

proot kills its tracees when it exits or crashes (atexit and the handlers
for SIGSEGV, SIGABRT and the like), but a SIGKILLed proot runs neither.
Android SIGKILLs single processes of an app: its phantom process killer
trims the oldest child processes once there are more than 32 on the phone,
or one that uses much CPU in the background, and the kernel's OOM killer
picks one process too. The tracees then run on untraced, and every syscall
the seccomp filter sends to the tracer returns ENOSYS. An idle shell exits
on its failed read, but a shell waiting for a command it ran loops on
wait4() forever at full CPU, its child left a zombie.

PTRACE_O_EXITKILL (Linux 3.8) makes the kernel SIGKILL each tracee when
its tracer exits, however it ends. New tracees inherit it with the other
options.

diff --git a/src/compat.h b/src/compat.h
--- a/src/compat.h
+++ b/src/compat.h
@@ -135,6 +135,9 @@
 #    ifndef PTRACE_O_TRACESECCOMP
 #        define PTRACE_O_TRACESECCOMP	0x00000080
 #    endif
+#    ifndef PTRACE_O_EXITKILL
+#        define PTRACE_O_EXITKILL	0x00100000
+#    endif
 #    ifndef PTRACE_EVENT_FORK
 #        define PTRACE_EVENT_FORK	1
 #    endif
diff --git a/src/tracee/event.c b/src/tracee/event.c
--- a/src/tracee/event.c
+++ b/src/tracee/event.c
@@ -527,7 +527,14 @@
 				PTRACE_O_TRACEVFORKDONE	|
 				PTRACE_O_TRACEEXEC	|
 				PTRACE_O_TRACECLONE	|
-				PTRACE_O_TRACEEXIT);
+				PTRACE_O_TRACEEXIT	|
+				/* The kernel SIGKILLs every tracee when
+				 * proot ends, even by a SIGKILL, which
+				 * kill_all_tracees() can't catch: an
+				 * untraced tracee gets ENOSYS from each
+				 * syscall the seccomp filter sends to
+				 * the tracer and can spin forever.  */
+				PTRACE_O_EXITKILL);
 
